mean event times.\", \"source_ids\": [\"final.metric.grokking_incidence\", \"final.metric.mean_final_accuracy\", \"final.metric.restricted_mean_delay\"], \"citation_keys\": [], \"evidence_refs\": [\"paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/metrics\", \"source_evidence/task/evaluate_final.py#L1066\"]}\n{\"claim\": \"The descriptive mean of the five observed final studied endpoints is0.878640, distinct from the failure-weighted registry functional.\", \"source_ids\": [\"final.evidence.episodes\"], \"citation_keys\": [], \"evidence_refs\": [\"paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes\", \"derived/summary.json#/final_observed_endpoint_mean\"]}\n{\"claim\": \"Related development settings are(0.003,1,1),(0.003,1,0.5),(0.006,0.5,0.5); the faster setting has an unavailable width256 seed211 record, not a measured zero or known failure cause.\", \"source_ids\": [\"result.top_program_01\", \"result.top_program_02\"], \"citation_keys\": [], \"evidence_refs\": [\"paper_data.json#/all_programs/0/evaluation_evidence/episodes\", \"paper_data.json#/all_programs/1/evaluation_evidence/episodes\", \"paper_data.json#/all_programs/2/evaluation_evidence/episodes\"], \"source_scope_note\": \"Selection IDs identify related selected configurations only. All sensitivity numbers and missingness are supported by explicit raw registry pointers, not these scalar IDs.\"}\n{\"claim\": \"The evaluated source uses CPU float32, full-batch AdamW, deterministic algorithms, at most two CPU threads and one inter-op thread; requirements pin numpy2.1.3 and torch2.5.1+cpu.\", \"source_ids\": [\"final.evidence.episodes\"], \"citation_keys\": [], \"evidence_refs\": [\"source_evidence/task/evaluate_final.py#L765\", \"source_evidence/task/evaluate_final.py#L781\", \"source_evidence/task/requirements.txt\"]}\n{\"claim\": \"The readable final evaluator digest matches the registry evaluator digest; hash agreement is provenance, while code contents support architecture and optimizer details.\", \"source_ids\": [\"final.evidence.episodes\"], \"citation_keys\": [], \"evidence_refs\": [\"derived/source_manifest.json\", \"source_evidence/task/evaluate_final.py\", \"paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluator_sha256\"]}\n{\"claim\": \"Recorded selected-development seed evaluation durations are981/754 seconds, and final seed totals3199/2794/3488 seconds after rounding; incomplete final coverage prevents extrapolating complete-grid runtime.\", \"source_ids\": [\"final.evidence.episodes\", \"result.top_program_01\"], \"citation_keys\": [], \"evidence_refs\": [\"paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes\", \"paper_data.json#/best_correct/evaluation_evidence/episodes\", \"derived/summary.json#/runtime_by_scope_seconds\"]}\n{\"claim\": \"All five retained final studied endpoints have training accuracy1.0, with different residual train cross-entropies; initial/final global norms increase in every record, including delayed-event records. Table norms/losses are individual measured endpoints, not a norm-trajectory mediation test.\", \"source_ids\": [\"final.evidence.episodes\"], \"citation_keys\": [], \"evidence_refs\": [\"paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes\", \"derived/observations.json#/rows\", \"derived/norm_loss_records.tex\"]}\n{\"claim\": \"Power et al. document delayed generalization on small algorithmic datasets.\", \"source_ids\": [\"ref.arxiv.2201.02177\"], \"citation_keys\": [\"Power2022GrokkingGB\"], \"evidence_refs\": [\"source_evidence/literature/2201.02177_opening.txt\"]}\n{\"claim\": \"Nanda et al. reverse-engineer a Fourier-based modular-addition computation in small Transformers; our architecture and measurements do not establish the same mechanism.\", \"source_ids\": [\"ref.arxiv.2301.05217\"], \"citation_keys\": [\"Nanda2023Progress\"], \"evidence_refs\": [\"source_evidence/literature/2301.05217_opening.txt\"]}\n{\"claim\": \"Liu et al. relate grokking to loss landscapes as a function of weight norm.\", \"source_ids\": [\"ref.arxiv.2210.01117\"], \"citation_keys\": [\"Liu2022OmnigrokGB\"], \"evidence_refs\": [\"source_evidence/literature/2210.01117_opening.txt\"]}\n{\"claim\": \"Varma et al. propose differing learning speeds and norm efficiencies of memorizing and generalizing circuits.\", \"source_ids\": [\"ref.arxiv.2309.02390\"], \"citation_keys\": [\"Varma2023ExplainingGT\"], \"evidence_refs\": [\"source_evidence/literature/2309.02390_opening.txt\"]}\n{\"claim\": \"Kumar et al. study lazy-to-rich dynamics, including polynomial regression exhibiting grokking without regularization.\", \"source_ids\": [\"ref.arxiv.2310.06110\"], \"citation_keys\": [\"Kumar2023GrokkingAT\"], \"evidence_refs\": [\"source_evidence/literature/2310.06110_opening.txt\"]}\n{\"claim\": \"Davies et al. connect grokking and double descent through pattern-learning speeds and capacity variation.\", \"source_ids\": [\"ref.arxiv.2303.06173\"], \"citation_keys\": [\"Davies2023Unifying\"], \"evidence_refs\": [\"source_evidence/literature/2303.06173_opening.txt\"]}\n{\"claim\": \"Nakkiran et al. document nonmonotone generalization as model size or duration varies; the present narrow sweep does not establish double descent.\", \"source_ids\": [\"ref.arxiv.1912.02292\"], \"citation_keys\": [\"Nakkiran2020Double\"], \"evidence_refs\": [\"source_evidence/literature/1912.02292_opening.txt\"]}\n{\"claim\": \"AdamW decouples weight decay from adaptive loss-gradient updates; nominal shrinkage is not a measured complete dynamical clock.\", \"source_ids\": [\"ref.arxiv.1711.05101\"], \"citation_keys\": [\"Loshchilov2019AdamW\"], \"evidence_refs\": [\"source_evidence/literature/1711.05101_opening.txt\"]}\n\npaper_strategy.json\ntop-level: ['status', 'selected_prompt_family', 'recommended_title', 'central_question', 'central_thesis', 'narrative_rationale', 'prior_paper_story_status', 'edit_framing_decision', 'staged_input_impact', 'method_groups', 'results_focus', 'figure_plan', 'figure_specs', 'supplementary_plan', 'forbidden_headings', 'forbidden_phrases', 'notes_for_writer', 'failure_reason']\ncentral_thesis \"The retained comparisons show earlier fitting at larger widths without monotone short-horizon generalization, while two longer-horizon width-128 delayed events remain conditional observations rather than qualified evidence of a size law or a decay-clock mechanism.\"\n\npaper_data.json\ntop-level: ['ablation_studies', 'all_programs', 'best_any', 'best_correct', 'evidence_sources', 'final_evaluation', 'generated_at', 'grounding_sources', 'idea_titles', 'improvement_trace', 'paper_profile', 'presentation_contract', 'results_dir', 'top_programs', 'totals']\nablation_studies list 0\nall_programs list 3\nbest_any dict ['attempt_dir_name', 'attempt_id', 'combined_score', 'correct', 'eligible', 'eval_index', 'evaluation_evidence', 'idea_dir_name', 'idea_id', 'program_dir', 'program_id', 'program_idx']\nbest_correct dict ['attempt_dir_name', 'attempt_id', 'combined_score', 'correct', 'eligible', 'eval_index', 'evaluation_evidence', 'idea_dir_name', 'idea_id', 'program_dir', 'program_id', 'program_idx']\nevidence_sources dict ['ablations', 'investigation']\nfinal_evaluation dict ['correct', 'evaluation_evidence', 'evaluator_sha256', 'limitations', 'manifest_path', 'metrics', 'outcome', 'program_tree_sha256', 'results_tree_sha256', 'status', 'task_tree_sha256']\ngenerated_at str 2026-11-13T03:55:03.438098+00:00\ngrounding_sources dict ['final.evidence.episodes', 'final.metric.complete_episode_fraction', 'final.metric.control_validity_rate', 'final.metric.evidence_score', 'final.metric.grokking_incidence', 'final.metric.mean_final_accuracy', 'final.metric.restricted_mean_delay', 'final.qualification.correct', 'final.qualification.outcome', 'final.qualification.status', 'result.best_any_score', 'result.best_correct_score', 'result.improvement_001', 'result.improvement_002', 'result.top_program_01', 'result.top_program_02', 'result.total_attempts', 'result.total_correct_programs']\nidea_titles list 3\nimprovement_trace list 2\npaper_profile str standalone\npresentation_contract dict ['forbidden_visible_terms', 'internal_fields', 'preferred_terms', 'run_unit', 'threshold_rate_rule', 'variant_unit']\nresults_dir str work/results/t02/codex/20261112_215258/investigation\ntop_programs list 2\ntotals dict ['attempts', 'correct_programs', 'evaluated_programs', 'ideas']\n\nreferences_provenance.json\ntop-level: ['count', 'generated_at', 'references', 'queries', 'scope_limitation']\ncount 8\ngenerated_at \"2026-11-13T04:37:33.692320+00:00\"\nscope_limitation \"The strategy limits consultation to eight authorized originals. The requested minimum of 25 references cannot be met without broadening that contract; unrelated retrieved records were excluded, not cited to fill a quota.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
