['limitations'])\nprint('Protected hashes:',{path:hashlib.sha256(Path(path).read_bytes()).hexdigest() for path in ['paper.tex','references.bib','references_provenance.json']})\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"Sections: ['Introduction', 'Related Work', 'Method', 'Results', 'Discussion and Limitations', 'Conclusion', 'Supplementary Information']\nCited keys: ['Davies2023Unifying', 'Kumar2023GrokkingAT', 'Liu2022OmnigrokGB', 'Loshchilov2019AdamW', 'Nakkiran2020Double', 'Nanda2023Progress', 'Power2022GrokkingGB', 'Varma2023ExplainingGT']\nUnresolved citation keys: []\nBibliography keys without provenance: []\nLiterature-grounded claims: 8\nCitation-linked evidence files missing: []\nnotes_for_writer: This stage produces a strategy only. Do not draft paper.tex, claims_grounding.json, run new training, generate figures, retrieve literature, or run final-paper validation here.\nnotes_for_writer: VENUE.md selects ICLR 2026, anonymous conference paper, 8-9 body pages excluding references. The inspected supplied paper.sty is single-column with 5.5in textwidth and 9in textheight. full_width therefore means the full single column, not a two-column figure*. There is no distinct narrow conference column to target. Retain selected formatting; the age comments in the supplied style do not independently certify current official-template provenance, which must be checked before final submission without changing geometry to fit content.\nnotes_for_writer: Private-only campaign guardrail: no downstream_study or study.* sources exist. Do not infer scored/unscored attempt counts or score improvements, or import an unavailable campaign baseline. Compare the actual fixed-reference arms instead. The locally inspected controller configuration and final record configuration agree; do not imply a broader independent source-freeze audit than the supplied evidence supports.\nnotes_for_writer: Private-only aggregate semantics: final.metric.grokking_incidence=0.2222222222222222 is a nine-cell design-weighted aggregate; it is not an unbiased population event probability. final.metric.mean_final_accuracy=0.48813319164009916 includes failure weighting, not the mean of five recorded endpoint accuracies. final.metric.restricted_mean_delay=0.9458333333333333 is a normalized capped functional, not an observed mean time-to-generalization. Keep these aggregates out of headline figures; if retained in an audit table, define the weighting and do not label absent values measured zero.\nnotes_for_writer: The reference differs from the studied condition in learning rate and initialization. The zero-decay intervention has finite-horizon scope. Initial-global-norm matching does not match capacity, function, representations, or effective regularization; at width128 it is identical to the studied condition. No circuit, lazy-to-rich transition, random-label control, frozen-feature control, width-by-decay grid, or positive-decay clock collapse was measured.\nnotes_for_writer: Literature scope is restricted to authorized starter originals. references.bib and references_provenance.json contain retrieval metadata, not proof that a paper was read; check identities and consult only allowed original works before citation. Use Power for the phenomenon, Loshchilov/Hutter for AdamW, Liu for norm hypotheses, and permitted Kumar/Varma/Nanda/Davies/Nakkiran originals only where needed as distinct theoretical or architectural comparators. Do not inspect citation neighborhoods, recommendations, or unidentified related-work hits, and do not infer the forbidden paper identity.\nnotes_for_writer: After references insert a page break and Supplementary Information with substantive grounded subsections; include a separate LLM Usage section there. Preserve anonymization and omit author identities, acknowledgements, funding, and self-identifying links. Route authoritative later appendix-ranked analyses to the supplement without retroactively editing this strategy or hiding essential evidence.\nstaged_input_impact: downstream_study and study.* grounding sources are absent. Do not invent campaign-level selection margins, scored/unscored counts, or a campaign baseline comparison. Use the configuration explicitly present in final records and the measured fixed-reference arms.\nFinal outcome: completed not_qualified False\nFinal limitations: ['Final evaluation completed but did not qualify; search success does not establish final qualification.', 'Non-qualification may reflect performance, uncertainty, validity, adaptivity, or other criteria; report only causes supported by evaluator evidence.', 'Retained metrics do not independently establish claims whose qualification or validity checks failed. Missing gate diagnostics remain unknown.']\nProtected hashes: {'paper.tex': 'b3ff7797b3a82319e93238b6b735d10fd397ca6e703e7ca9e0a87ad5a0e0b9d3', 'references.bib': '3b68b7718a61921376ce9e634d8050eee9eb52ba0944c1aa29fdc41872e16a54', 'references_provenance.json': '9542a7fcd6afd69e868dbeb9946e73b54eeb12e7e045aaad5bccf50b8d2a10d8'}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"sed -n '1,18p' global_memory_summary.md; sed -n '119,142p' paper.tex; sed -n '158,192p' paper.tex; sed -n '273,309p' paper.tex; tail -n 22 memory.md; if [ -f global_memory/conclusions.md ]; then cat global_memory/conclusions.md; fi; sed -n '1,100p' .codex/skills/memory-log/scripts/append_memory.py\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"sed -n '1,18p' global_memory_summary.md; sed -n '119,142p' paper.tex; sed -n '158,192p' paper.tex; sed -n '273,309p' paper.tex; tail -n 22 memory.md; if [ -f global_memory/conclusions.md ]; then cat global_memory/conclusions.md; fi; sed -n '1,100p' .codex/skills/memory-log/scripts/append_memory.py\"","aggregated_output":"# Global Memory Summary\n\nUse as qualitative context only; do not use as quantitative grounding source.\n\n## Recent Entries\n\n- 2026-11-12 | step=idea | scope=idea\n  - summary: Selected Separating Width Effects from the Post-Fit Decay Clock; idea_bundle_written and execution_pending. gate=kept; trigger=none; reason=No experimental evidence or validated refinement is available; an untested design is not a scientific conclusion.\n  - evidence: The validated manifest reports combined_score=0.7779622741764081 and correct=true; histories and prior memory have no experimental results. The referenced baseline source was unavailable, which does not establish a protocol defect. Considered a descriptive width-only sweep and capacity-confounded frozen-feature controls; selected a directly runnable paired width-by-decay intervention with censoring-aware analysis. No training, evaluator execution, computational probes, package installation, or web access occurred. Canonical local memory target is ideas/01_separating_width_effects_from_the_post_fit_decay_clock/memory.md; no alternate cycle-local target was created.\n- 2026-11-12 | step=verify | scope=idea\n  - summary: Manually checked matching rubric content and one canonical local memory target; clarified immediate events, exact event-rate intervals, and informative-censoring limitations. gate=kept; trigger=none; reason=Prospective safeguards do not constitute experimental findings.\n  - evidence: Both bundles share four rubric objects; the three implementation verifications contain five, six, and five executable literal snippets. Only ideas/01_separating_width_effects_from_the_post_fit_decay_clock/memory.md was used for local memory. No computational validation or experimental execution occurred.\n- unknown_ts | step=unknown_step | scope=unknown_scope\n  - summary: (missing summary)\n  - evidence: (missing evidence)\n- unknown_ts | step=unknown_step | scope=unknown_scope\n  - summary: (missing summary)\n  - evidence: (missing evidence)\n\\toprule\nSeed & Width 32 & Width 128 & Width 256 \\\\\n\\midrule\n60613 & C & D & M \\\\\n70717 & C & D & M \\\\\n80821 & C & M & M \\\\\n\\bottomrule\n\\end{tabular}\n% @evidence[[paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes]]\n\\end{table}\n\nThe final evaluation completed but did not qualify. We preserve that conclusion rather than interpreting selection as scientific acceptance. No supplied diagnostic distinguishes a statistical/performance failure from a validity or adaptivity failure. Retained observations can describe the measured trajectories, but they cannot restore claims that would require qualification. In particular, neither complete trajectories in individual cells nor successful execution of local controls establishes general validity of the final comparison.\n% @evidence[[paper_data.json#/grounding_sources/final.qualification.status]]\n% @evidence[[paper_data.json#/grounding_sources/final.qualification.outcome]]\n% @evidence[[paper_data.json#/grounding_sources/final.qualification.correct]]\n\n\\subsection{Width Accelerates Fitting but Does Not Order Short-Horizon Accuracy}\nThe short-horizon comparisons show a consistent fitting order. In the studied condition, width-32 fitting onsets are 2,200 and 2,800 updates; width 128 fits at 300 updates in both seeds; width 256 fits at 200 in both seeds. The paired widest-minus-narrowest differences are thus $-2,000$ and $-2,600$ updates. Yet held-out endpoint accuracy is highest at width 32, lowest at width 128, and intermediate at width 256 in each seed (Table~\\ref{tab:development}, Figure~\\ref{fig:endpoint}). Earlier training fit therefore does not order generalization at this horizon.\n% @evidence[[derived/summary.json#/cells]]\n% @evidence[[derived/summary.json#/paired/development_256_minus_32]]\n\n\\begin{table}[t]\n\\centering\n\\caption{Studied condition at the 6,000-update development horizon. Accuracy is mean $\\pm$ sample SD over the two seeds, in percent. Onsets are listed by seed rather than averaged with unobserved values. No sustained held-out onset is observed at any width.}\n\n\\begin{figure}[t]\n\\centering\n\\includegraphics[width=\\textwidth]{figures/width_endpoint_comparison.pdf}\n\\caption{Matched-condition endpoint comparisons. (a) Development observations at 6,000 updates. (b) Retained final observations at 24,000 updates. Each dot is a recorded seed; no missing cell is plotted at zero. The panels use different seeds and disjoint input pools, so their contrast is not a duration-only intervention. At width 128, norm matching duplicates the studied scientific trajectory; horizontally separated symbols do not denote independent evidence.}\n\\label{fig:endpoint}\n% @evidence[[derived/observations.json#/rows]]\n\\end{figure}\n\n\\subsection{Retained Delayed Events at Intermediate Width}\nAt the final horizon, the two retained width-128 studied trajectories first fit at 300 and 200 updates and first satisfy the sustained held-out threshold at 17,600 and 19,200 updates, respectively. Their observed delays are therefore 17,300 and 19,000 updates. Their endpoints are 98.353\\% and 97.768\\%. In contrast, width-32 fitting onsets are 2,600, 2,400, and 3,000 updates, with no sustained held-out onset by 24,000 updates; endpoints are 80.925\\%, 88.842\\%, and 73.433\\%. Figure~\\ref{fig:onsets} separates these delayed events from right censoring and missing records.\n% @evidence[[paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes]]\n% @evidence[[derived/observations.json#/rows]]\n\nFor the two shared final seeds, width-128 minus width-32 endpoint differences are 17.428 and 8.927 percentage points. This is a conditional intermediate-versus-narrow comparison. The widest-versus-narrowest final comparison is unavailable, and all final seed-level contrasts requiring the complete width set are absent from the supplied summary. It would be inappropriate to present the retained intermediate-width advantages as a complete ordering of model sizes or an estimate of a general width effect.\n% @evidence[[derived/summary.json#/paired/final_128_minus_32]]\n% @evidence[[paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes]]\n\nConditional on the retained records, the delayed-event counts are two of two at width 128 and zero of three at width 32. Exact 95\\% binomial intervals are approximately $[0.158,1]$ and $[0,0.708]$. These wide intervals make the uncertainty visible even under an independent-seed assumption; missingness and failed qualification impose additional limits that such intervals do not repair. They are neither a significance result nor evidence that width-32 models can never generalize. The design-weighted final event fraction, two of nine, uses a different denominator and must not be confused with either conditional fraction.\n% @evidence[[derived/summary.json#/cells/final_128]]\n% @evidence[[derived/summary.json#/cells/final_32]]\n% @evidence[[paper_data.json#/grounding_sources/final.metric.grokking_incidence]]\n\n\\begin{figure}[t]\n\\centering\n\\includegraphics[width=\\textwidth]{figures/fit_and_generalization_onsets.pdf}\n\\caption{Training-fit and held-out onsets for the studied condition. Each vertical offset identifies a seed within a width. A circle is sustained training fit; a star is sustained held-out onset; an arrow indicates a recorded trajectory whose held-out onset is censored at the horizon. Missing trajectories receive no arrow. Onsets require three consecutive checkpoints at 0.99 training or 0.95 held-out accuracy. Panel axes deliberately differ because the horizons differ.}\n\\label{fig:onsets}\n% @evidence[[derived/observations.json#/rows]]\n% @evidence[[source_evidence/task/evaluate_final.py#L1001]]\n\\end{figure}\n\n\\subsection{What the Matched Controls Do and Do Not Explain}\nRemoving decay produces strong training/evaluation separation within the measured budget. In the retained final no-decay controls, width-32 held-out endpoints range from 0.478\\% to 0.797\\%, and both width-128 endpoints are zero. Nevertheless, training-fit onsets are 1,300--1,600 updates at width 32 and 200 updates at width 128. These measured configuration contrasts support a substantial finite-horizon difference between training fit and generalization with and without decay. They do not establish that weight decay is necessary for grokking in another architecture, task, optimizer, or training horizon.\n% @evidence[[derived/observations.json#/rows]]\n% @evidence[[source_evidence/task/evaluate_final.py#L821]]\n\n\\subsection{Complete Retained Final Comparisons}\n\\begin{table}[h]\n\\centering\n\\caption{All retained final condition endpoints and onsets. S: studied; R: reference; Z: no decay; N: norm matched. Onset values are updates. The $>24000$ notation means no sustained held-out onset was recorded; it is not an extrapolated event time. All listed training onsets are observed. Missing width--seed cells are given separately in Table~\\ref{tab:coverage}, not inserted as zero-valued rows.}\n\\label{tab:allfinal}\n\\small\n\\begin{tabular}{rrrrrr}\n\\toprule\nSeed & Width & Arm & Accuracy (\\%) & Fit & Onset \\\\\n\\midrule\n60613 & 32 & S & 80.925 & 2600 & $>24000$ \\\\\n60613 & 32 & R & 59.352 & 9100 & $>24000$ \\\\\n60613 & 32 & N & 67.747 & 3400 & $>24000$ \\\\\n60613 & 32 & Z & 0.478 & 1600 & $>24000$ \\\\\n60613 & 128 & S & 98.353 & 300 & 17600 \\\\\n60613 & 128 & R & 84.272 & 700 & $>24000$ \\\\\n60613 & 128 & N & 98.353 & 300 & 17600 \\\\\n60613 & 128 & Z & 0.000 & 200 & $>24000$ \\\\\n70717 & 32 & S & 88.842 & 2400 & $>24000$ \\\\\n70717 & 32 & R & 54.570 & 11100 & $>24000$ \\\\\n70717 & 32 & N & 50.797 & 4500 & $>24000$ \\\\\n70717 & 32 & Z & 0.744 & 1400 & $>24000$ \\\\\n70717 & 128 & S & 97.768 & 200 & 19200 \\\\\n70717 & 128 & R & 80.659 & 700 & $>24000$ \\\\\n70717 & 128 & N & 97.768 & 200 & 19200 \\\\\n70717 & 128 & Z & 0.000 & 200 & $>24000$ \\\\\n80821 & 32 & S & 73.433 & 3000 & $>24000$ \\\\\n80821 & 32 & R & 65.037 & 9600 & $>24000$ \\\\\n80821 & 32 & N & 70.829 & 3400 & $>24000$ \\\\\n80821 & 32 & Z & 0.797 & 1300 & $>24000$ \\\\\n\\bottomrule\n\\end{tabular}\n% @evidence[[derived/observations.json#/rows]]\n\\end{table}\n\n- next_action: Rerun strategy-only consistency checks and record final status; no final paper validation, drafting, figure generation, experiments, or network access.\n\n### 2026-11-13T04:12:07.547355+00:00 | step=final | scope=paper\n- summary: paper_strategy.md and paper_strategy.json ready; stop_reason=framing_complete_strategy_checks_passed; gate=kept; trigger=none; reason=No new experimental recommendation established by framing.\n- evidence: Final strategy-only checks passed: JSON contract, existing source identifiers, memo agreement, explicit completed/not_qualified/false qualification,5/9 final coverage, two retained width128 delayed events, observed right censoring versus missingness, norm-arm metric identity, matched short-horizon width comparisons, single-column5.5in geometry, three bounded figures including one early concept overview,8.8-page allocation, and five substantive supplementary subsections. Selected bounded width/fitting/generalization framing beats untested clock collapse, universal size laws, and recency-driven optimization narratives. No manuscript, claims file, figures, new training, final-paper validation, literature retrieval, or network access produced.\n- next_action: Downstream writer should implement the thesis-first plan and source-linked plots, consult only permitted original references before citation, disclose failed qualification prominently, and retain all missingness, censoring, uncertainty, and attribution limits during writing/review/audit/revision.\n\n### 2026-11-13T04:15:09.220619+00:00 | step=paper | scope=paper\n- summary: Adopted conditional width/fitting/generalization framing; final qualification failure retained; gate=kept; trigger=none; reason=framing and source audit do not establish a new scientific recommendation.\n- evidence: final.qualification.* reports completed/not_qualified/false. Five final width-seed records survive, 3/2/0 by width. Local evaluate_final.py SHA256 matches final evaluator hash exactly. Supplied bibliography has off-scope retrieval contamination and only four of eight planned starter originals; the strategy restricts consultation to eight authorized originals, conflicting with the requested 25-reference minimum.\n- next_action: Snapshot readable evaluated sources; consult eight exact authorized originals only; generate per-seed comparisons and a detailed censored-results paper. Explicitly flag the bibliography-count conflict rather than adding unconsulted or irrelevant sources.\n\n### 2026-11-13T04:32:03.935264+00:00 | step=draft | scope=paper\n- summary: Drafted a source-linked standalone width study with failed final qualification and explicit missingness; gate=kept; trigger=none; reason=additional descriptive diagnostics do not identify a new causal recommendation.\n- evidence: paper.tex now contains 8 body pages in the rendered draft, two vector comparison figures, final availability and seed-level tables, and endpoint norm/loss diagnostics from retained final curves. Recomputed onsets agree with recorded events. 35 mapped claims validate with8 consulted original references; scientific-evidence currently has zero dangling links. Bibliography minimum25 remains unsatisfied under the eight-original framing restriction. Canonical figure validation imports an absent host module; compile guard rejects a normal system TeX symlink, while direct sanitized compilation succeeds.\n- next_action: Finish reproducibility and provenance artifacts, inspect PDF and plots, rerun evidence and rendered-supplement checks, and report unresolved production constraints without upgrading scientific qualification.\n\n### 2026-11-13T04:42:32.507020+00:00 | step=final | scope=paper\n- summary: paper.tex and claims_grounding.json are consistent with the inspected grounded inputs; stop_reason=grounded_outputs_written_production_requirements_unresolved; gate=kept; trigger=none; reason=descriptive writing and audit do not establish a new mechanistic recommendation.\n- evidence: Produced paper.tex, compiled12-page paper.pdf with8 body pages, claims_grounding.json with35 mapped claims, figure_manifest.json, reproducibility/code/source bundles, and validation_report.json. All four table fragments regenerate exactly and are embedded in the manuscript. Scientific-evidence verification:176 links,80 resolved,96 anchored,0 dangling,14 manifests. Independent final qualification remains completed/not_qualified/false; cause unknown. Source citations corrected to actual controller constants atL37 and onset extraction atL1001. Development claims use explicit raw registry pointers rather than selection scores. Two quantitative composites inspected at full text width; required concept overview is wired with a guarded orchestrator-owned placeholder. Section/citation/claim checks and rendered SI pass. Local rendered body span is93.1percent on page8, not a replacement for parent geometry validation. Full production validation is not claimed:8 consulted originals cannot meet25-reference minimum under the framing restriction; host figure module is absent and canonical compile guard rejects a normal system TeX symlink.\n- next_action: Orchestrator should render the overview and run authoritative host layout/figure validation. Resolve the scoped-literature/reference-quota conflict before treating delivery as complete. Preserve qualification failure, missingness, censoring, and unknown diagnostics through all later revisions; do not add unsupported claims or new evaluations.\n\nRetain reduced initialization as the current common-configuration starting point: it improved aggregate terminal accuracy in the recorded comparison while delayed-generalization incidence stayed at zero, so treat this as a finite-horizon search lead, not evidence that initialization mediates model-size effects or that grokking occurred. Use common-configuration interventions allowed by the reset/plan contract; resolving width dependence, uncertainty, or decay-clock mechanisms requires publicly supplied width-, arm-, or seed-resolved observations, not reconstruction of evaluator internals.\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Append validated local/global memory entries for idea workflows.\n\nTwo modes:\n\n* default (event append) — appends one memory event to ``memory.md`` (local +\n  global) plus one JSONL record to ``memory.jsonl``. Existing behavior.\n* ``--write-conclusions`` — atomically replaces ``conclusions.md`` with a\n  validated single-paragraph distilled summary and appends a record to\n  ``conclusions_history.jsonl``. Validation rejects empty input,\n  multi-paragraph input, or input over 300 words.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport fcntl\nimport json\nimport os\nimport stat\nimport sys\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Any\n\nCONCLUSIONS_WORD_LIMIT = 300\nGATE_TRIGGER_VALUES = (\"a\", \"b\", \"c\", \"d\")\n\nLOCAL_MEMORY_HEADERS = \"\"\"# Memory Log\n\n## Context\n## Idea Discoveries\n## Program Evaluations\n## Failures / Regressions\n## Next Hypotheses\n\"\"\"\n\nGLOBAL_MEMORY_HEADER = \"# Global Memory Log\\n\\n\"\n\n\ndef utc_now() -> str:\n    \"\"\"Return the current UTC timestamp string.\"\"\"\n    return datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat()\n\n\ndef _load_event(*, event_json: str | None, event_file: Path | None) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Load event.\"\"\"\n    if event_json:\n        parsed = json.loads(event_json)\n    elif event_file is not None:\n        parsed = json.loads(event_file.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n    else:\n        raw = input().strip()\n        if not raw:\n            raise ValueError(\"missing event payload\")\n        parsed = json.loads(raw)\n    if not isinstance(parsed, dict):\n        raise ValueError(\"event payload must be a JSON object\")\n    return parsed\n\n\ndef _ensure_required_fields(event: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Ensure required fields.\"\"\"\n    normalized = dict(event)\n    if not isinstance(normalized.get(\"timestamp\"), str) or not normalized[\"timestamp\"].strip():\n        normalized[\"timestamp\"] = utc_now()\n\n    required_string_fields = (\"step\", \"scope\", \"summary\", \"evidence\", \"next_action\")\n    for key in required_string_fields:\n        value = normalized.get(key)\n        if not isinstance(value, str) or not value.strip():\n            raise ValueError(f\"missing required string field: {key}\")\n        normalized[key] = value.strip()\n\n    for key in (\"idea_id\", \"attempt_id\", \"program_id\"):\n        value = normalized.get(key)\n        if value is None:\n            continue\n        if not isinstance(value, str):\n            normalized[key] = str(value)\n        normalized[key] = normalized[key].strip() or None\n\n    metrics = normalized.get(\"metrics\")\n    if metrics is not None and not isinstance(metrics, dict):\n        raise ValueError(\"metrics must be an object when present\")\n    rubrics = normalized.get(\"rubrics\")\n    if rubrics is not None and not isinstance(rubrics, list):\n        raise ValueError(\"rubrics must be an array when present\")\n    tags = normalized.get(\"tags\")\n    if tags is not None:\n        if not isinstance(tags, list):\n            raise ValueError(\"tags must be an array when present\")\n        normalized[\"tags\"] = [str(item).strip() for item in tags if str(item).strip()]\n    return normalized\n\n\ndef _markdown_entry(event: dict[str, Any]) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Handle markdown entry logic for this module.\"\"\"\n    lines = [\n        f\"### {event['timestamp']} | step={event['step']} | scope={event['scope']}\",\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
